  "raw": {
    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DSQ561/lecturer-senior-lecturer-in-audiology-2-year-fixed-term": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Audiology",
      "description": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Audiology - 2 Year Fixed Term at De Montfort University Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Audiology - 2 Year Fixed Term De Montfort University Location: Leicester Salary: £39,906 to £56,535 Hours: Full Time Contract Type: Fixed-Term/Contract Placed On: 18th August 2026 Closes: 28th October 2026 Job Ref: 602 Job Location: Gateway House Employee Weekly Hours: 37.00 Market Supplement: Job Description: Main duties and responsibilities Faculty / Directorate De Montfort University (DMU) is a vibrant, ambitious and inclusive learning institution. We have been awarded the ‘Collaborative Award for Teaching Excellence’ from Advance HE for the work around Decolonising DMU and are the first university to receive the silver award in the Race Equality Charter (REC). The Faculty of Health and Life Sciences at De Montfort University educates and develops professionals who make a significant difference to people’s lives, health, wellbeing and society. It is home to the Leicester School of Allied Health Sciences in which this post will be based. Role You would work as part of a team, primarily delivering high-quality teaching and training across a range of programmes. In addition to adult aural diagnostics and rehabilitation, we are seeking expertise in anatomy and physiology of the auditory pathway and/or acoustics. You would contribute to teaching and training across our programmes, including the development and delivery of new programmes and short courses. The role will also involve being a key member of the academic placement team, supporting both students on placement and placement providers. The Audiology section of the school is one of the largest in the country and boasts excellent facilities with the latest clinical equipment. It offers an excellent opportunity for engagement in enterprise activities and research. Ideal Candidate The ideal candidate should be experienced and be enthusiastic about the subject. They should possess a broad foundation in audiology and be able to contribute across a range of teaching and training activities. While a postgraduate qualification in Audiology would be advantageous, we are interested to hear from candidates with substantial clinical experience. The candidate must be passionate about teaching and training, demonstrate creativity, and be committed to developing and expanding professional networks. To view the job description and person specification, please click here Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Ok Ok PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Manage your job alerts Manage your job alerts Account Verification Missing In order to create multiple job alerts, you must first verify your email address to complete your account creation Request verification email Request verification email jobs.ac.uk Account Required In order to create multiple alerts, you must create a jobs.ac.uk jobseeker account Create Account Create Account Alert Creation Failed Unfortunately, your account is currently blocked. Please login to unblock your account. Login Login Email Address Blocked We received a delivery failure message when attempting to send you an email and therefore your email address has been blocked. You will not receive j