    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DSO336/digital-content-and-media-technical-instructor-performance-and-events": {
      "title": "Digital Content and Media Technical Instructor (Performance and Events)",
      "description": "Digital Content and Media Technical Instructor (Performance and Events) at De Montfort University Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Digital Content and Media Technical Instructor (Performance and Events) De Montfort University Location: Leicester Salary: £32,080 to £38,784 Hours: Part Time Contract Type: Permanent Placed On: 10th August 2026 Closes: 4th September 2026 Job Ref: 621 33.3 hours per week Main duties and responsibilities About De Montfort University De Montfort University (DMU) is recognised for its innovative teaching, industry partnerships, world-leading research, and excellent student experience. We offer over 300 courses, many with professional accreditation and strong industry links, preparing students for successful careers. Digital Content and Media Technical Instructor Join our Digital and Technology Team and play a key role in supporting teaching, performances, and events across the University. You'll provide specialist technical expertise, maintain industry-standard facilities, and help create exceptional learning experiences for students. Key Responsibilities Provide technical support for Drama, Dance, Acting, and other creative disciplines. Support conferences, performances, and internal and external events. Support teaching, rehearsals, assessments, and public performances. Deliver technical workshops and one-to-one student support. Advise academic staff on technical solutions. Maintain lighting, sound, video, and stage equipment. Work with Estates, Events, and Digital & Technology teams to deliver high-quality services. Carry out equipment maintenance, PAT testing, and maintain technical records. Maintain venue specifications and support digital signage across campus. Support occasional evening and weekend events. What You'll Do No two days are the same. You could be delivering technical workshops, supporting student performances, advising academics, supporting the tech for a conference and event, preparing venues for commercial hire, or maintaining specialist performance facilities Working with the Team Leader and Technical Instructors, you'll collaborate with colleagues across the University to deliver outstanding technical support for teaching, learning, performances, and events. About You Essential A qualification in Technical Theatre, Live Events, Production Technology, Performing Arts Technology, or equivalent experience. Experience operating lighting, sound, video, and stage technologies. Experience supporting live performances, teaching, or events. Experience maintaining technical equipment and working safely. Excellent communication, organisation, and problem-solving skills. A proactive, customer-focused approach with the ability to work independently and as part of a team. Flexibility to support evening and weekend activities. Desirable Experience delivering technical workshops or practical training. If you're passionate about technical theatre, live events, and supporting student success, we'd love to hear from you. To view the job description and person specification, please click here Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Ok Ok PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Manage your job alerts Manage your job alerts Account Verification Missing In order to create mu