    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DST570/senior-exams-and-awards-officer": {
      "title": "Senior Exams and Awards Officer",
      "description": "Senior Exams and Awards Officer at De Montfort University Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Senior Exams and Awards Officer De Montfort University - Registry Services Location: Leicester Salary: £39,906 to £43,482 Hours: Full Time Contract Type: Permanent Placed On: 28th August 2026 Closes: 20th September 2026 Job Ref: 654 Job Description: Main duties and responsibilities Why Join De Montfort University? At De Montfort University (DMU), we are committed to delivering an outstanding experience at every stage of the student journey, from registration through to graduation. We are seeking an experienced and highly organised Senior Exams and Awards Officer to play a key role in delivering examinations, awards and graduation ceremonies. You will work at the heart of the University’s academic operations, taking responsibility for complex and time-critical activities that matter to our students. You will help plan and coordinate exam periods and graduation ceremonies, ensuring that services are delivered accurately, efficiently and with a strong focus on the student experience. You will also supervise and support colleagues within the Exams and Awards team, managing workloads and priorities throughout the year. You will join a university recognised globally for its commitment to the UN Sustainable Development Goals, working on a vibrant campus in the heart of Leicester. Role As Senior Exams and Awards Officer, you will support the Exams and Awards Manager in leading the operational planning and delivery of exams, graduation ceremonies, and awards. Your responsibilities will include: Managing the team, allocating workloads and priorities and supporting colleagues to deliver an efficient, student-focused service. Coordinating exam periods, including scheduling, venues, exam papers, invigilation and arrangements for students with additional requirements. Working with colleagues across Registry, faculties, Estates, IT and other services to deliver exams effectively. Supporting the recruitment, training and allocation of exam invigilators. Keep this one as it is. Supporting graduation ceremonies, working with internal teams and external suppliers to coordinate arrangements. Overseeing graduation processes, including ticketing, communications, publications and certificate distribution. Identifying process improvements and opportunities to use digital tools to improve efficiency and service quality. Managing competing deadlines and responding constructively to operational issues. Working flexibly during exam and graduation periods, including some evening and weekend working. About You You will be an experienced operational professional with strong organisational, people management and problem-solving skills, comfortable working in a busy environment with changing priorities. In particular, you will: Experience of managing or supervising staff, allocating work, setting priorities and monitoring performance. Experience of planning and delivering complex operational activities. Excellent organisational and problem-solving skills, with the ability to work under pressure and to tight deadlines. Experience of delivering professional, customer-focused services and a commitment to an excellent student experience. Ability to build productive relationships with colleagues and stakeholders. Strong digital skills and an interest in using technology to improve service delivery. Experience of identifying and implementing process improvements. Ability to communicate confidently and diplomatically with a range of audiences. Confidence in supporting colleagues through change and developing new ways of working. To view the job description and person specification, please click here Contact For an informal discussion about the role, please contact Emily Maddock Khan, Head of Student Journey, at emily.maddockkhan@dmu.ac.uk Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Ok Ok PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Manage your job alerts Manage your job alerts Account Verification Missing In order to create multiple job alerts, you must first verify your email address to complete your account creation Request verification email Request verification email jobs.ac.uk Account Required In order to create multiple alerts, you must create a jobs.ac.uk jobseeker account Create Account Create Account Alert Creation Failed Unfortunately, your account is currently blocked. Please login to unblock your account. Login Login Email Address Blocked We received a delivery failure message when attempting to send you an email and therefore your email address has been blocked. You will not receive job alerts until your email address is unblocked. To do so, please choose from one of the two options below. Re-verify your email Update your email Re-verify your email Update your email Max Alerts Reached A maximum of 5 Job Alerts can be created against your account. Please remove an existing alert in order to create this new Job Alert Manage your job alerts Manage your job alerts Creation Failed Unfortunately, your alert was not created at this time. Please try again. Ok Ok Create PhD Alert Create Job Alert When you create this PhD alert we will email you a selection of PhDs matching your criteria. When you create this job aler