    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DSS587/technician-in-digital-print-textiles": {
      "title": "Technician in Digital Print (Textiles)",
      "description": "Technician in Digital Print (Textiles) at De Montfort University Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Technician in Digital Print (Textiles) De Montfort University - Technical Services Location: Leicester Salary: £26,707 to £31,236 Hours: Part Time Contract Type: Permanent Placed On: 25th August 2026 Closes: 8th September 2026 Job Ref: 655 Job Description: Main duties and responsibilities Technical Services Grade D 0.8 FTE Annualised Hours De Montfort University (DMU) is seeking a skilled and enthusiastic Digital Textile Print Technician to join our Technical Services team. This is an exciting opportunity to support students, academics and researchers within our creative and specialist textile facilities. Working within our textile workshops, you will play a key role in the operation and maintenance of our digital textile printing facilities, supporting teaching, learning and project work across a range of programmes. You will provide expert advice, practical demonstrations and technical support to students and staff, ensuring equipment is used safely, effectively and to the highest standards. The Role Operating and maintaining large-format Mimaki digital textile printers and associated software. Supporting students and academic staff with fabric printing, textile production and technical processes. Demonstrating specialist equipment, techniques and workflows. Managing print bookings and maintaining accurate production records. Assisting with workshop preparation, equipment maintenance and stock control. Promoting safe working practices and supporting Health & Safety compliance, including risk assessments and COSHH procedures. Contributing to open days, outreach events and wider technical services activities. Ideal Candidate An HND, relevant technical qualification, or substantial practical experience in a related field. Experience operating large-format Mimaki textile printers and associated digital print software. Excellent technical skills and a strong attention to detail. Experience working within a workshop, studio or technical environment. Strong communication skills and the ability to explain technical information to a range of users. A commitment to maintaining high standards of service, safety and customer support. The following would be advantageous: Experience of traditional textile dyeing and printing techniques. Experience working within a Further or Higher Education environment. Experience developing safe working procedures and technical protocols. To view the job description and person specification, please click here Contact For further datail please contact Robert Leary ( Chief Technical Instructor) robert.leary@dmu.ac.uk Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Ok Ok PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Manage your job alerts Manage your job alerts Account Verification Missing In order to create multiple job alerts, you must first verify your email address to complete your account creation Request verification email Request verification email jobs.ac.uk Account Required In order to create multiple alerts, you must create a jobs.ac.uk jobseeker account Create Account Create Account Alert Creation Failed Unfortunately, your account is currently blocked. Please login to unblock your accou