    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DSP375/lecturer-in-digital-technology-and-design": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Digital Technology & Design",
      "description": "Lecturer in Digital Technology & Design at De Montfort University Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Lecturer in Digital Technology & Design De Montfort University - Faculty of Technology, Arts & Culture Location: Leicester Salary: £39,906 to £43,482 Hours: Part Time Contract Type: Permanent Placed On: 13th August 2026 Closes: 3rd September 2026 Job Ref: 642 Job Description: Main duties and responsibilities De Montfort University (DMU) is an ambitious, globally minded institution with a relentless focus on delivering quality teaching and learning, and a campus-wide focus on providing a sector-leading student experience. A culturally rich university with a palpable commitment to the public good, it strives to maintain a stimulating and inclusive environment where staff and students are able to thrive. The university is a vibrant, multicultural hub of learning, creativity and innovation that never surrenders to convention. Our success is built on a fantastic student experience coupled with award-winning teaching and world-class facilities that help students develop the skills and attitudes employers’ demand. Faculty / School This role is within the Design Subject Area, in the School of Design Innovation, in the Faculty of Technology, Arts and Culture. The subject area consists of three distinct but inter-related areas – Design Crafts, Product Design and Interior Design, with the applicant being based in the Product Design team but working across the subject area for a significant part of their role. The Role This role is critical to curriculum delivery, the School’s Digital Transformation agenda and to the University’s future-facing ambitions under Imagine 2031 . It will deliver essential, core 2D and 3D CAD teaching (Solidworks, Photoshop, Illustrator, InDesign) and develop capability in Life Cycle Assessment (LCA) software for the Design Subject area. A willingness to learn and develop proficiency in additional subject-specific software, including AutoCAD, SketchUp and Rhino would be beneficial. Support will be provided as required. The post will also require broader technology integration skills including 3D printing, scanning, VR, generative AI. These areas of expertise will underpin emerging and future roles and core competencies for our graduates in the design sector. These will include digital materials specialists, circularity analysts, sustainable product technologists, computational designers and immersive‑environment creators. As this role cross teaches through subject area, it is hoped the applicant will foster closer collaboration between the subjects and bring insights to the delivery teams about where collaboration can be found. Ideal Candidate We are looking for an experienced and ambitious lecturer within the subject area of Design, with specific expertise in digital design software, visual communication and current industrial design practices. You will have experience of current industry software, teaching in Higher Education, and be expected to contribute to the future and ongoing development of the design subject area. You will have access to a range of training opportunities and facilities relevant to your on-going professional development/practice and the ability to develop and maintain your own scholarly and/or professional profile. To view the job description and person specification click here Informal enquires about the position to Nicky Harding, Subject Group Lead for Design & Materials. Contact Nicola.harding@dmu.ac.uk Contact Informal enquires about the position to Nicky Harding, Subject Group Lead for Design & Materials. Contact Nicola.harding@dmu.ac.uk Competencies Curriculum Development Teaching Delivery Assessment & Feedback Student Support External Engagement Quality Assurance Technology Integration Professional Development Skills Communication Empathy Critical Thinking Time Management Adaptability Collaboration Honest and Compassionate Innovative and Creative Community Minded Education BSc / BA Degree Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Ok Ok PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Manage your job alerts Manage your job alerts Account Verification Missing In order to create multiple job alerts, you must first verify your email address to complete your account creation Request verification email Request verification email jobs.ac.uk Account Required In order to create multiple alerts, you must create a jobs.ac.uk jobseeker account Create Account Create Account Alert Creation Failed Unfortunately, your account is currently blocked. Please login to unblock your account. Login Login Email Address Blocked We received a delivery failure message when attempting to send you an email and therefore your email address has been blocked. You will not receive job alerts until your email address is unblocked. To do so, please choose from one of the two options below. Re-verify your email Update your email Re-verify your email Update your email Max Alerts Reached A maximum of 5 Job Alerts can be created against your account. Please remove an existing alert in order to create this new Job Alert Manage your job alerts Manage your job alerts Creation Failed Unfortunately, your alert was not created at this time. Please try again. Ok Ok Create PhD