    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DSL459/lecturer-senior-lecturer-in-probation-and-community-justice": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Probation and Community Justice",
      "description": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Probation and Community Justice at De Montfort University Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Probation and Community Justice De Montfort University Location: Leicester Salary: £39,906 to £56,535 Hours: Full Time, Part Time Contract Type: Permanent, Fixed-Term/Contract Placed On: 31st July 2026 Closes: 25th September 2026 Job Ref: 604 Job Location: Gateway House Employee Weekly Hours: 37.00 Market Supplement: Job Description: Main duties and responsibilities Full-time (3 x 2-year fixed-term posts) and 0.5 FTE permanent post Faculty / Directorate De Montfort University (DMU) is an ambitious, globally minded and culturally rich university with a strong commitment to the public good. We strive to maintain a stimulating and inclusive environment that champions difference, celebrates success and transforms lives through education, research and partnership. By joining the Community Justice team within the School of Applied Social Sciences, you will help prepare the next generation of professionals entering the criminal justice system with the knowledge, skills and values to make a meaningful difference to individuals, communities and society. Following the successful re-award of our contract with His Majesty's Prison and Probation Service (HMPPS), which we have delivered for over 30 years, we are seeking enthusiastic academics and practitioners to join our established Community Justice team. Role We are seeking to appoint highly motivated and committed Lecturers or Senior Lecturers in Community Justice to join our team. We have three full-time, two-year fixed-term posts and one 0.5 FTE permanent post available. Please indicate within your application which post(s) you wish to be considered for. You will contribute to the delivery, development and enhancement of our Community Justice and Probation programmes, teaching predominantly through innovative online and blended learning approaches. You will design and deliver engaging learning experiences, support students through personal tutoring, contribute to assessment and feedback, and work collaboratively with colleagues and external partners to ensure an outstanding student experience. You will also contribute to curriculum development, scholarship and wider academic activity within the School. This is an exciting opportunity to join one of the UK's leading Community Justice education teams, delivering nationally recognised programmes in partnership with His Majesty's Prison and Probation Service and helping to shape the future probation workforce. Ideal Candidate You will hold an honours degree and a postgraduate qualification in Community Justice, Criminology or a related discipline, or an appropriate professional probation qualification. You will have experience of learning and development within higher education or professional practice in probation, community justice or a related criminal justice setting. You will be an excellent communicator with strong organisational skills and the ability to build effective working relationships with colleagues, students and His Majesty's Prison and Probation Service. Experience of online or blended learning would be advantageous. Appointments will be made at the Lecturer or Senior Lecturer level, depending on qualifications, experience, and evidence of academic leadership. Above all, you will share DMU's commitment to providing an outstanding, inclusive and supportive learning experience for all students and be passionate about developing the next generation of probation professionals. To view the job description and person specification for Lecturer in Community Justice, please click here To view the job description and person specification for Senior Lecturer in Community Justice, please click here Contact For more information about these roles, please contact Ravinderjit Kaur Briah at rbriah@dmu.ac.uk or by calling 0116 257 7827. Education BSc / BA Degree Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Ok Ok PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Manage your job alerts Manage your job alerts Account Verification Missing In order to create multiple job alerts, you must first verify your email address to complete your account creation Request verification email Request verification email jobs.ac.uk Account Required In order to create multiple alerts, you must create a jobs.ac.uk jobseeker account Create Account Create Account Alert Creation Failed Unfortunately, your account is currently blocked. Please login to unblock your account. Login Login Email Address Blocked We received a delivery failure message when attempting to send you an email and therefore your email address has been blocked. You will not receive job alerts until your email address is unblocked. To do so, please choose from one of the two options below. Re-verify your email Update your email Re-verify your email Update your email Max Alerts Reached A maximum of 5 Job Alerts can be created against your account. Please remove an existing alert in order to create this new Job Alert Manage your job alerts Manage your job alerts Creation Failed Unfortunately, your alert was not created at this time. Please try again. Ok Ok Create PhD Alert Create Job Alert When you creat