    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DSS771/project-and-administration-assistant": {
      "title": "Project & Administration Assistant",
      "description": "Project & Administration Assistant at De Montfort University Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Project & Administration Assistant De Montfort University Location: Leicester Salary: £26,707 to £31,236 Hours: Full Time Contract Type: Permanent Placed On: 26th August 2026 Closes: 11th September 2026 Job Ref: 627 Job Location: Gateway House Employee Weekly Hours: 37.00 Market Supplement: Job Description: Main duties and responsibilities Marketing and Communications Directorate: The Directorate offers full-service marketing and communications support to the university, comprising brand and creative development; design and print services; corporate and student recruitment marketing campaigns; CRM (Customer Relationship Management) and conversion campaigns; faculty marketing and recruitment; reputation management; media relations and public affairs; internal and external communications engagement; events; admissions, schools and colleges engagement; widening participation; enquiry management and follow up; web and digital development and market insight. The Role: The Project and Administration Assistant is a role which will be crucial in providing project and administrative support to the Marketing and Communications directorate and members of the directorate’s Senior Leadership Team (SLT). This role will be key in supporting the SLT across a diverse range of projects and deliverables, ensuring that we are successfully delivering our work in supporting The Empowering University Strategy. You will help with undertaking research; reviewing data; producing and collating key project documentation and information; implementing project governance and co-ordinating activities to ensure the directorate meets its objectives and deadlines. The role will also assist in wider administrative duties such as supporting with arranging project meetings; helping with travel and event organisation; setting up and servicing key meetings, including taking meeting notes, supporting on developing key paperwork; as well as assisting in producing papers for relevant boards and committees. The role will also particularly help to support areas such as finance, budget management, HR and Health and Safety, ensuring these operate smoothly. You will understand the variety of work across the directorate and ensure you work collaboratively with colleagues both within, and external, to the directorate to ensure successful delivery. Stakeholder management and relationship building will be an important part of the role. You will be expected to participate in key institutional events and initiatives as required. Ideal Candidate: The ideal candidate will possess strong collaboration, communication and organisational skills, with a proven track record of project management. It is essential that you are able to work collaboratively and possess the ability to successfully develop and manage positive stakeholder relationships, including the ability to influence and negotiate, as required. You must have strong experience in providing administration support, including arranging and servicing meetings, assisting on events and drafting and collating papers. You will need to be comfortable with utilising data and insight to inform decision making. You should feel comfortable working flexibly across a number of activities, with a range of colleagues, as well as being able to work independently, using your own initiative to achieve your objectives. The ideal candidate will be diligent and detailed focused, with a pro-active, innovative and positive approach to work. To view the job description and person specification, please click here Skills Attention to Detail Time Management Communication Problem-Solving Collaboration Adaptability Initiative Honest and Compassionate Accountability Organisation Reliability Resilience Teamwork Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Ok Ok PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Manage your job alerts Manage your job alerts Account Verification Missing In order to create multiple job alerts, you must first verify your email address to complete your account creation Request verification email Request verification email jobs.ac.uk Account Required In order to create multiple alerts, you must create a jobs.ac.uk jobseeker account Create Account Create Account Alert Creation Failed Unfortunately, your account is currently blocked. Please login to unblock your account. Login Login Email Address Blocked We received a delivery failure message when attempting to send you an email and therefore your email address has been blocked. You will not receive job alerts until your email address is unblocked. To do so, please choose from one of the two options below. Re-verify your email Update your email Re-verify your email Update your email Max Alerts Reached A maximum of 5 Job Alerts can be created against your account. Please remove an existing alert in order to create this new Job Alert Manage your job alerts Manage your job alerts Creation Failed Unfortunately, your alert was not created at this time. Please try again. Ok Ok Create PhD Alert Create Job Alert When you create this PhD alert we will email you a selection of PhDs matching your criteria. When you create this job alert we will email 