    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DSS134/technical-instructor-biomedical-engineering-06-fte": {
      "title": "Technical Instructor (Biomedical Engineering) 0.6 FTE",
      "description": "Technical Instructor (Biomedical Engineering) 0.6 FTE at De Montfort University Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Technical Instructor (Biomedical Engineering) 0.6 FTE De Montfort University - Technical Services Location: Leicester Salary: £32,080 to £38,784 Hours: Part Time Contract Type: Permanent Placed On: 24th August 2026 Closes: 13th September 2026 Job Ref: 652 Job Description: Main duties and responsibilities About the Role As a Technical Instructor, you will play a key role in supporting practical teaching sessions, laboratory-based learning and project work within biomedical and other engineering disciplines. You will be responsible for maintaining specialist biomedical engineering equipment, preparing laboratory activities, and providing guidance to students on the use of equipment and technical procedures. You will contribute to the ongoing development of technical facilities and support innovation in teaching practices, ensuring that laboratories remain fit for purpose and aligned with industry standards. Key Responsibilities Support the delivery of practical teaching, laboratory sessions and project-based learning. Prepare, set up and maintain biomedical engineering laboratories and equipment. Provide technical instruction and guidance to students and staff. Ensure compliance with health and safety legislation, risk assessments and safe systems of work. Maintain laboratory equipment and coordinate servicing, calibration and repairs. Assist with the procurement and management of laboratory consumables, equipment and resources. Support student projects, final-year dissertations and research activities where appropriate. Contribute to the continuous improvement of laboratory practices, facilities and technical services. Undergo necessary training if required on medical equipment. Role We are looking for a proactive and student-focused individual with: A degree, HND or equivalent qualification in Biomedical Engineering, Medical/Clinical Engineering, Electronics, Mechanical Engineering or a related discipline. Experience working with laboratory, engineering or medical technology / equipment. Knowledge of biomedical engineering principles and practical applications. Excellent organisational and problem-solving skills. Strong communication skills and the ability to work effectively with students, academic colleagues and external stakeholders. A commitment to health and safety and delivering high-quality technical support. Willingness to learn and professional development. Team player, and willingness to support open days. Experience of working within higher education, healthcare technology, clinical engineering or a research environment would be advantageous To view the job description and person specification click here Contact For further information please contact Ashok Karavadra email: akaravadra@dmu.ac.uk , contact no: 01162078060 Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Ok Ok PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Manage your job alerts Manage your job alerts Account Verification Missing In order to create multiple job alerts, you must first verify your email address to complete your account creation Request verification email Request verification email jobs.ac.uk Account Required In order 